{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   THE KEPT EVIDENCE TILE — the upload component's finished state, drawn once.

   A file already attached and a file that arrived a second ago must be the same
   box, or a record's card shows two kinds of tile for the same thing. That box
   is the upload component's `.upl-tile.done`, and this file is the only place it
   is written: a consuming module calls `kept()` rather than retyping the markup,
   and the tile the controller draws after a POST draws the same states from the
   same words.
   → assets/controllers/upload_controller.js

   TWO THINGS THIS FILE IS:

     1. kept(f) — THE DATA CONTRACT. A hash, so a module with its own evidence
        model fills it from whatever it has.

     2. entry(file, detailUrl) — the same contract, filled from a FileEntry.

   THE STATES. The storage makes ONE ~400px picture per photograph and serves it
   through the permission check; a tile with that picture shows it, and a tile
   without says which of the three reasons applies — in the storage's own words,
   from ThumbStateEnum, never retyped here:

     made   the picture fills the tile, and the tile opens the file
     wait   the camera glyph and a pill saying the picture is being made
     failed the same glyph and a pill saying none could be made — the original is
            untouched and still downloadable
     none   a document or a track: its own glyph and ground, and no pill, because
            there was never a picture to make

   A TILE WITH NOTHING TO LOOK AT IS NOT OPENABLE. Only a made thumbnail links,
   which is also why the link is the `.sh` layer rather than the tile: a removal
   is a <button> and may not sit inside an <a>. Where there is no removal the
   whole cell is the link instead.

   THE VOCABULARY IS THE SHELL'S `.upl-*`, shipped in shell.css. Nothing here
   defines a class, a token or an inline style.
   ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}

{# THE DATA CONTRACT.

   Required: name. Everything else is optional and the tile draws the honest
   absence rather than a blank.

   Keys:
     name        the file's own name — the picture's alt text, and the default label
     label       what to print under the tile; defaults to name
     key         the storage key. Present ⇒ the removal is drawn and the tile is a
                 <span>; absent ⇒ nothing may be removed and the cell is the link
     thumbState  made | wait | failed | none — ThumbStateEnum's own values
     thumbUrl    the ~400px picture through the serving route, or '' if none
     detailUrl   the file's own page, or '' where the host ships no Files hub
     title       the tile's own hover sentence, where a surface has one to add #}
{% macro kept(f) %}
    {%- set state = enum('Uhifadhi\\Storage\\Enum\\ThumbStateEnum').tryFrom(f.thumbState|default('none')) ?? enum('Uhifadhi\\Storage\\Enum\\ThumbStateEnum').Nothing -%}
    {%- set picture = 'made' == state.value and f.thumbUrl|default('') -%}
    {%- set label = f.label|default(f.name) -%}
    {%- set page = picture ? f.detailUrl|default('') : '' -%}
    {%- set removable = f.key|default('') -%}
    {%- set shape = {'made': 'shot', 'wait': 'making', 'failed': 'nothumb', 'none': 'doc'}[state.value] -%}
    {#- Only a picture earns the flat photo ground; a made state with no URL to
        draw is the same tile as one whose picture could not be made. -#}
    {%- set shape = 'shot' == shape and not picture ? 'nothumb' : shape -%}

    {#- With a removal in the way the cell cannot be an <a>, so the picture layer
        carries the link; with nothing to remove the whole cell carries it. -#}
    {%- set tag = page and not removable ? 'a' : 'span' -%}
    <{{ tag }} class="upl-tile done {{ shape }}"{% if 'a' == tag %} href="{{ page }}"{% endif %}
        {%- if f.title|default('') %} title="{{ f.title }}"{% endif %}>
        {%- if picture -%}
            {%- set layer = page and 'span' == tag ? 'a' : 'span' -%}
            <{{ layer }} class="sh"{% if 'a' == layer %} href="{{ page }}"{% endif %}><img src="{{ f.thumbUrl }}" alt="{{ f.name }}" loading="lazy"></{{ layer }}>
        {%- elseif 'none' == state.value -%}
            {{ ux_icon('storage:file', {width: 20, height: 20}) }}
        {%- else -%}
            {{ ux_icon('storage:camera', {width: 22, height: 22}) }}
            <span class="th">{{ state.label }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        <span class="fn">{{ label }}</span>
        {%- if removable -%}
            <button type="button" class="rm" data-upl-remove data-upl-key="{{ f.key }}" aria-label="Remove this evidence">&times;</button>
        {%- endif -%}
    </{{ tag }}>
{% endmacro %}

{# The same contract, filled from a FileEntry.

   detailUrl is PASSED rather than generated, for the reason the preview states:
   the file's own page exists only where the host runs the Files hub.
   → templates/overlay/_preview.html.twig #}
{% macro entry(file, detailUrl) %}
    {%- import _self as evidence -%}
    {{- evidence.kept({
        name: file.name,
        key: file.key,
        thumbState: file.thumbState.value,
        thumbUrl: file.hasThumbnail ? path('storage_evidence_show', {key: file.thumbKey}) : '',
        detailUrl: detailUrl,
    }) -}}
{% endmacro %}
